# Longor architecture boundaries

- `SRD.md` is the source of truth for Longor architecture, milestone claims, and
  VLA service contract. If a change modifies those contracts, update `SRD.md`
  first and map code changes to that update.
- Enforce the runtime contract exactly as defined in `SRD.md` (module layout,
  dependency direction, env facade behavior, planner/executor/runner boundaries,
  and VLA service wire contract).
- Keep source layout flat under `src/`, with simulation backends only under
  `src/envs/`. Do not introduce `core/`, `sim/`, `vla/`, `robots/`, registries,
  or backend-protocol abstractions.
- Keep backend-specific runtime details out of general modules: references to
  policy/backend names belong only in `src/envs/**`, `services/**`, and
  `src/config.py`.
- Keep Linux-only sim dependencies lazily imported so non-sim modules stay
  importable on any host.
